       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6400 mg a day is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen, and each 1600 mg dose is twice the maximum single dose. I wouldn't enter this for any requester without a documented clinical reason that a prescriber and pharmacist had reviewed.\n- **You're still not the prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed clinician who is responsible for the patient's care.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. **Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team** so they can assess the patient and write an appropriate order.\n2. **Involve pharmacy** if there's a reason someone thinks a very high dose is needed. They can review it and suggest safer options.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives me an order within safe limits, I can enter it right away."
